      "text": "To find the value of \\( n \\) such that \\( 173 \\cdot 927 \\equiv n \\pmod{50} \\), we can use modular arithmetic properties. We start by reducing the numbers modulo 50.\n\nFirst, we reduce 173 modulo 50:\n\\[ 173 \\div 50 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 23, \\]\nso\n\\[ 173 \\equiv 23 \\pmod{50}. \\]\n\nNext, we reduce 927 modulo 50:\n\\[ 927 \\div 50 = 18 \\text{ remainder } 27, \\]\nso\n\\[ 927 \\equiv 27 \\pmod{50}. \\]\n\nNow we need to find the product of these reduced numbers modulo 50:\n\\[ 173 \\cdot 927 \\equiv 23 \\cdot 27 \\pmod{50}. \\]\n\nWe calculate \\( 23 \\cdot 27 \\):\n\\[ 23 \\cdot 27 = 621. \\]\n\nNext, we reduce 621 modulo 50:\n\\[ 621 \\div 50 = 12 \\text{ remainder } 21, \\]\nso\n\\[ 621 \\equiv 21 \\pmod{50}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) is\n\\[ \\boxed{21}. \\]",
